  "_read": "every deviation is an integer number of bf16 ULPs at the local logit magnitude. The arithmetic is the same; only the GEMM tiling changed. p = softmax over two logits has |dp/dlogit| <= 0.25, so a 1-ULP logit difference is worth up to ~0.03 of score -- which is the entire observed score deviation and is why bit-equality of scores is unreachable for any shape-changing refactor in bf16."
